---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SOURCES, METHOD_NOTE } from '../data/sources';
import { creatures, CREATURE_COUNT, DATA_VERSION } from '../data/creatures';

const ko = creatures.filter((c) => c.tameMethod === 'knockout').length;
const passive = creatures.filter((c) => c.tameMethod === 'passive').length;
const special = creatures.filter((c) => c.tameMethod === 'special').length;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Data & Sources - How ARKTools Computes Every Number"
  description="How ARKTools is built: game-file constants from the ARK Smart Breeding project, formulas documented on the ARK Community Wiki, unit-tested against hand-worked examples. Full source list and coverage."
  path="/sources"
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow"><Icon name="scroll-text" size={15} /> Provenance</span>
    <h1>Data &amp; Sources</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {METHOD_NOTE.replace(/\s+/g, ' ')}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2 class="with-icon"><Icon name="book-open-text" size={20} /> Where the numbers come from</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data">
        <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Used for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {SOURCES.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td><a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.name}</a></td>
              <td style="white-space:normal">{s.what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size:.85rem">
      Game-file constants via the MIT-licensed
      <a href="https://github.com/cadon/ARKStatsExtractor" rel="noopener">ARK Smart Breeding</a>
      values set (v{DATA_VERSION}); formulas from its published Taming.cs and
      StatValueCalculation, cross-checked against ark.wiki.gg. Retrieved October 2026.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2 class="with-icon"><Icon name="list-checks" size={20} /> Coverage - {CREATURE_COUNT} creatures, honestly labeled</h2>
    <div class="stat-grid" style="margin-bottom:1rem">
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Knockout tames</span><span class="stat__value">{ko}</span><span class="stat__sub">full simulation</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Passive tames</span><span class="stat__value">{passive}</span><span class="stat__sub">wake-tame multipliers</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__label">Special mechanics</span><span class="stat__value">{special}</span><span class="stat__sub">documented, not simulated</span></div>
    </div>
    <p>
      This site deliberately ships a <strong>curated subset</strong> of the most-tamed
      creatures rather than all 1000+ species, so every number can be verified.
      Creatures with unique taming mechanics (Wyvern milk, Rock Drake venom, Reaper
      gestation, Titanosaur starvation, Carcharodontosaurus corpse feeding) are listed
      with their mechanics but excluded from the standard food-affinity calculator - 
      a food table would be actively wrong for them.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data">
        <thead><tr><th>Creature</th><th>Method</th><th>Preferred kibble</th><th>Egg tier</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {creatures.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <td><strong>{c.name}</strong></td>
              <td><span class={`badge badge--${c.tameMethod}`}>{c.tameMethod}</span></td>
              <td>{c.preferredKibble ? `${c.preferredKibble} Kibble` : '-'}</td>
              <td>{c.eggSize ?? '-'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h2 class="with-icon"><Icon name="microscope" size={20} /> Verification</h2>
    <p>
      The math libraries are unit-tested (vitest) against hand-worked examples,
      including values the community knows cold: a level 150 Rex needs exactly
      17 Exceptional Kibble and finishes at level 224 at 1x; a level 150 Tusoteuthis
      needs 200 Black Pearls; two clean parents have a 7.31% chance of at least one
      mutation; a perfect 150-tame tops out at 225.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Found a number that disagrees with your in-game result? Damage taken during a
      tame lowers effectiveness, server settings may differ from the defaults, and
      ASA rebalances some constants - all of which sit outside this model by design.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
